## Exact entry and deadline ledger

Read-only input check (already run once):

```sh
bash /root/lane-trn-tools/reader-native-bounded-v1/entry.sh --check-config
```

Prepared native entry, for the separately reviewed native opportunity ONLY:

```sh
bash /root/lane-trn-tools/reader-native-bounded-v1/entry.sh --execute
```

Use entry.sh, not a direct --execute Python invocation: the entry adds a kernel-
handled outer timeout (TERM at 295 seconds, KILL after 5 more). All durations
include startup, input checks, wait, fixture, Go, cleanup and evidence. The
Python work cutoff is 270 seconds; its owned cleanup calls end by 295 seconds,
leaving the final 5 seconds for records. A Go child including termination/reap
has at most min(170 seconds, the remaining work budget); its normal wait reserves
5 seconds for TERM/KILL/reap. Each package has a 75-second test timeout, serial
-p 1 and GOMAXPROCS=2. No compilation or worker starts after the work cutoff.
Python signals alone cannot guarantee timely handling of an uninterruptible
kernel/daemon operation; outer termination is a backstop, not native evidence.
The whole-lifetime bounds have arithmetic/mock validation only at this stage.

The first original carrier has one blocking kernel acquisition, at most 60
seconds; the second has one nonblocking acquisition. A second busy result closes
the first before writing evidence. Both are opened O_NOFOLLOW, without create,
truncate or unlink, and checked by regular type, UID, device, inode and path/fd
identity. Their immutable device/inode pairs remain 29/82 and 64512/7508772.
No workstation compilation is part of this artifact; the workstation busy rule
remains nonblocking exit 75 without another queue.

## Fixture and results

The exact original preflight/policy still checks Free >=3 GiB, Available >=12
GiB, disk >=15 GiB, full PSI avg10/avg60 <=5, and no competing heavy process.
A supplemental parser requires one complete valid full PSI row, rejecting
nonfinite, missing or duplicate values. PostgreSQL uses only the cached pinned
image, pull never, network none, loopback namespace, no host ports, 2 CPUs and
1 GiB. Both fixture families receive the same O_EXCL 0600 DSN file; inherited
fixture and processor overrides are cleared. Both test roots and the independent
real-reader subcase must pass, with both packages passing and no skips/failures.
The real reader/current-role/export/writer-exclusion assertions are unchanged.

Only a container with this invocation's exact name, ID, image, labels and limits
can be stopped/removed. Anonymous volumes are removed with that container and
read back; foreign scope, unresolved presence, remaining group/container/volume,
cleanup timeout or unreaped child prevents qualification. Every child has its
own process group, TERM/KILL/reap bounds and raw exit status. Go and PG logs use
files, inputs are hashed in blocks, and parsing is bounded. On a hard kill,
records may be partial; retain the outer raw status and inspect only the named
owned resources before making any cleanup claim. Permanent carriers are never
deleted. The private evidence directory and nonsecret logs are retained; its
DSN is removed on the normal bounded cleanup path.

Exit classifications: first carrier busy 73; second busy 74; resource refusal
78; child/test/timeout/cleanup failure 1 with distinct kind, phase and raw child
status. A child returning 75 is CHILD_FAILED, not a lock classification. No
in-round reacquisition or body retry occurs. The bounded readiness probe is the
existing fixture's startup check, not a native-body retry.

